post.description:
Generate streaming answers for queries using AI agents. This endpoint provides real-time
streaming responses for question answering with optional user personalization.

Simply provide a query string and optionally a `filter.collectionIds` array to get an AI-generated answer.
When `filter.collectionIds` is provided, those collections are included in the search scope, along with
any widget-based personalization collections when applicable. Otherwise, the endpoint uses the default
answer flow. The response is streamed using Server-Sent Events (SSE) format, allowing clients to receive
partial results as they are generated.

## Personalization

Pass the optional `user` object to enable personalized answers. When provided, the external
user record is upserted and their attributes are used to filter knowledge base collections
and tailor responses. At least one of `userId`, `email`, or `phone` is required within the
`user` object.

## Streaming vs Non-Streaming

Set `stream` to `false` to receive the full answer as a single JSON response instead of SSE
events. Defaults to `true`.

## Streaming Example

```javascript
const response = await fetch('https://api.brainfi.sh/v1/agents/answer', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'Authorization': 'Bearer bf_api_xxxxx',
    'agent-key': 'your-agent-key'
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    query: 'How do I reset my password?',
    user: { email: 'jane@example.com', properties: { plan: 'enterprise' } }
  })
});

const reader = response.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();

while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;

  const chunk = decoder.decode(value);
  const lines = chunk.split('\n');

  for (const line of lines) {
    if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {
      const event = JSON.parse(line.slice(6));

      switch (event.type) {
        case 'start':
          console.log('Answer started:', event.id);
          break;
        case 'progress':
          console.log('Progress:', event.content);
          break;
        case 'content':
          console.log('Content chunk:', event.content);
          break;
        case 'end':
          console.log('Answer completed:', event.conversationId);
          break;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

